---
/**
 * The turn as a loop. Two edges carry the argument: the request is rebuilt
 * from scratch on every pass (which is what makes curation possible), and a
 * mutating call parks at the approval gate before it runs.
 */
---

<figure class="koda-fig">
  <svg
    viewBox="0 0 880 512"
    role="img"
    aria-label="A turn is a loop. A user message enters, the request is assembled from scratch, streamed to the model, and if the model asked for tools each call is dispatched. Read-only calls run at once; mutating calls wait at an approval gate for y, a or n, and plan mode never reaches the gate because the write tools are not offered. Results are appended and the loop returns to assemble a fresh request. When the model asks for no tools, the turn ends."
  >
    <defs>
      <marker id="tl-a" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" fill="currentColor" />
      </marker>
      <marker id="tl-c" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" fill="var(--k-accent)" />
      </marker>
      <marker id="tl-w" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" fill="var(--k-warning)" />
      </marker>
    </defs>

    <!-- entry -->
    <text x="300" y="26" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor" fill-opacity=".78">you press enter</text>
    <line x1="300" y1="36" x2="300" y2="64" stroke="currentColor" stroke-opacity=".55" marker-end="url(#tl-a)" />

    <!-- assemble -->
    <rect x="150" y="68" width="300" height="56" rx="4" fill="var(--k-fill-accent)" stroke="var(--k-accent)" stroke-opacity=".7" />
    <text x="300" y="92" font-size="13.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--k-accent)">assemble the request</text>
    <text x="300" y="110" font-size="11.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor" fill-opacity=".85">prompt · skills · memory · history</text>

    <line x1="300" y1="124" x2="300" y2="158" stroke="currentColor" stroke-opacity=".55" marker-end="url(#tl-a)" />
    <text x="312" y="146" font-size="11.5" fill="currentColor" fill-opacity=".78">POST /v1/chat/completions</text>

    <!-- stream -->
    <rect x="150" y="162" width="300" height="56" rx="4" fill="var(--k-fill-quiet)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-opacity=".45" />
    <text x="300" y="186" font-size="13.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor">stream the completion</text>
    <text x="300" y="204" font-size="11.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor" fill-opacity=".85">text · reasoning · tool-call deltas</text>

    <line x1="300" y1="218" x2="300" y2="244" stroke="currentColor" stroke-opacity=".55" marker-end="url(#tl-a)" />

    <!-- branch -->
    <path d="M300 246 L378 278 L300 310 L222 278 z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-opacity=".5" />
    <text x="300" y="275" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor">tool</text>
    <text x="300" y="290" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor">calls?</text>

    <line x1="378" y1="278" x2="546" y2="278" stroke="currentColor" stroke-opacity=".55" marker-end="url(#tl-a)" />
    <text x="440" y="270" font-size="11.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor" fill-opacity=".78">none</text>
    <rect x="554" y="258" width="190" height="40" rx="4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-opacity=".45" />
    <text x="649" y="283" font-size="13" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor">the turn ends</text>

    <line x1="300" y1="310" x2="300" y2="344" stroke="currentColor" stroke-opacity=".55" marker-end="url(#tl-a)" />
    <text x="312" y="332" font-size="11.5" fill="currentColor" fill-opacity=".78">one or more</text>

    <!-- dispatch -->
    <rect x="150" y="348" width="300" height="56" rx="4" fill="var(--k-fill-quiet)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-opacity=".45" />
    <text x="300" y="372" font-size="13.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor">dispatch each call</text>
    <text x="300" y="390" font-size="11.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor" fill-opacity=".85">read-only calls run at once</text>

    <!-- the approval gate -->
    <path d="M450 364 L546 364" fill="none" stroke="var(--k-warning)" stroke-width="1.6" marker-end="url(#tl-w)" />
    <text x="498" y="357" font-size="11.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--k-warning)">mutating</text>

    <rect x="554" y="336" width="190" height="60" rx="4" fill="var(--k-fill-warn)" stroke="var(--k-warning)" stroke-opacity=".7" />
    <text x="649" y="359" font-size="13" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--k-warning)">approval gate</text>
    <text x="649" y="378" font-size="11.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor" fill-opacity=".9">y once · a always · n deny</text>

    <path d="M554 390 L450 390" fill="none" stroke="var(--k-warning)" stroke-width="1.6" marker-end="url(#tl-w)" />

    <text x="554" y="422" font-size="11.5" fill="currentColor" fill-opacity=".75">plan mode never reaches the gate —</text>
    <text x="554" y="438" font-size="11.5" fill="currentColor" fill-opacity=".75">the write tools are not offered at all.</text>

    <!-- the loop back -->
    <path d="M200 404 L200 452 L48 452 L48 96 L144 96" fill="none" stroke="var(--k-accent)" stroke-width="1.6" marker-end="url(#tl-c)" />
    <text x="212" y="456" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--k-accent)">results appended · the request is rebuilt from scratch</text>

    <text x="48" y="490" font-size="11.5" fill="currentColor" fill-opacity=".75">
      The loop runs up to max_steps (24). At the ceiling step_check asks the model whether work
    </text>
    <text x="48" y="506" font-size="11.5" fill="currentColor" fill-opacity=".75">
      remains, buying another budget, up to max_steps_hard (96).
    </text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>
    The cyan edge is why context curation is possible at all: the request is rebuilt on every
    pass, so trimming what gets sent never touches the conversation itself.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
